        "id": 2016993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-16T06:43:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Say that I\u0027m setting up Thread on Android. I need to know which interface (by name/index) is chosen as the upstream network.\n\nSo after registering the Thread\u0027s `NetworkAgent`, I need to register a `NetworkCallback` on Thread network to receive the `LocalNetworkInfo` to get the upstream network.\n\nThere\u0027s no interface name or interface index in `Network` object so I need to register a `NetworkCallback` for the `Network` in `LocalNetworkInfo`. But the problem is, I don\u0027t know how to construct a `NetworkRequest` that exactly matches this upstream network. I may still need to register the callback using the same `NetworkRequest` used as the upstream selector in `LocalNetworkConfig`. So I don\u0027t see how the returned upstream network can help in this case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "e5f717ed571c31b05fcf7b9285fadc78b184680e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6d42f8f_2b401f48",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/LocalNetworkInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-17T14:31:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea here is to do something like the following (simplified of course, but that\u0027s the idea)\n\n    val networkToIface \u003d mutableMapOf\u003cNetwork, String\u003e()\n\n    val cb \u003d NetworkCallback() {\n      override onLinkPropertiesChanged(net: Network, lp: LinkProperties) {\n        networkToIface.put(net, lp.getInterfaceName())\n      }\n      override onLost(net: Network) {\n        networkToIface.remove(net)\n      }\n    }\n    val nr \u003d NetworkRequest.Builder().addCapability(LOCAL_NETWORK).build()\n    connectivityManager.registerNetworkCallback(nr, cb)\n\n    fun getUpstreamIface(lni: LocalNetworkInfo) \u003d networkToIface[getUpstreamNetwork()];\n\nDoes this make sense ?",
      "parentUuid": "397d3814_ab742acc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "e5f717ed571c31b05fcf7b9285fadc78b184680e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
